From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:16:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/jm: allocate the command buffer descriptor pool on
 first use

The JM command buffer preallocated a 64 KiB descriptor BO in
panvk_create_cmdbuf(), before the command buffer is ever recorded.
dEQP-VK.api.command_buffers.allocate_many_primary/secondary allocate
10000 command buffers, which made that 625 MiB of GPU memory for empty
command buffers: on a 1 GiB Mali-G31 board deqp-vk was OOM-killed in
a 600 MB memory cgroup.

panvk_pool_alloc_mem() already allocates a backing BO when the pool has
none, and the CSF command buffers create all their pools without
prealloc, so do the same here.

Host (drm-shim, G31): allocate_many_primary maps 20000 64 KiB BOs
before, 0 after; execute_small/large_primary still pass.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
index 09cbf4a6611..90c4eda033a 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -487,7 +487,10 @@ panvk_create_cmdbuf(struct vk_command_pool *vk_pool, VkCommandBufferLevel level,
          panvk_device_adjust_bo_flags(device, PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_WB_MMAP),
       .slab_size = 64 * 1024,
       .label = "Command buffer descriptor pool",
-      .prealloc = true,
+      /* Allocated on first use, like the other pools: a 64 KiB BO per
+       * command buffer up front costs 640 MiB of GPU memory for the 10000
+       * command buffers of dEQP-VK.api.command_buffers.allocate_many_*. */
+      .prealloc = false,
       .owns_bos = true,
       .needs_locking = false,
    };
